    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BcwPa2LDQHuUgGQ3LvMYSa)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; it needs no other open PR.\n- Uses only `sp-reading--osascript` and `sp-devonthink-map`, which are already on `main`.\n- Merging it before or after the DEVONthink stack (#415 to #421, #451) is safe; the stack does not touch the new files.\n- The only shared line is one `(require ...)` in `sp-academic.el`; a conflict there is trivial.\n\n## What it does\n\n- Selecting text in DEVONthink's PDF viewer still needs DEVONthink's Highlight action; DEVONthink has no setting for \"highlight on select\".\n- This PR does that action for Sia, two ways:\n  - `C-c k d h` (`sp-devonthink-highlight-selection`): one key presses Highlight.\n  - `C-c k d H` (`sp-devonthink-auto-highlight-mode`): select in DEVONthink and nothing else; about two seconds later the selection is highlighted.\n- How the mode works:\n  - Looks at the front window's `selected text` every second, only while Emacs is not the focused app.\n  - Highlights once the same selection survived two looks, then not again until the selection is cleared.\n  - Stops itself with a message on any error.\n- How Highlight is pressed: `System Events` clicks the menu item named `Highlight` (`sp-devonthink-highlight-menu-item`), found by name in every menu.\n- Needs the Accessibility permission for Emacs.\n- Literate source: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-devonthink-autohighlight.org` (bullet lists).\n- 11 ERT tests cover the pure parts (settling, no repeats, re-arming, quoting, key bindings); the AppleScript was not run.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Open a PDF in DEVONthink, select a word, run `M-x sp-devonthink-highlight-selection`: the word is highlighted.\n- [ ] If it says there is no enabled \"Highlight\" item, check the real menu name and set `sp-devonthink-highlight-menu-item`.\n- [ ] If it says the Accessibility permission is missing, grant it to Emacs and retry.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-devonthink-auto-highlight-mode`, select text in DEVONthink, wait about two seconds: it is highlighted once.\n- [ ] Keep the selection: no second highlight is added.\n- [ ] Clear the selection and select the same words again: highlighted again.\n- [ ] While typing in Emacs the mode does nothing.\n- [ ] `C-c k d h` and `C-c k d H` work.\n- [ ] Check whether `selected text` works for a PDF in a tab or a separate viewer window (the mode only looks at window 1).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCNcBkSpRJxEkvTQ7P)_",
